On the way into and out of a page’s full screen, Ladybird changes only
the window’s full-screen state, so a maximized window stays maximized
underneath. Chromium does the same on X11, where SetFullscreen() of
its X11Window toggles only _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN (apart from a
workaround for Metacity). And on GTK, Gecko’s nsWindow calls only
gtk_window_fullscreen() and gtk_window_unfullscreen().
